      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Three series of 2-arylpyridothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-4-ones 3a-j, pyridothienotriazolopyrimidines 6-8 and 4-imino-pyridothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidines 9a,b were prepared to improve the pim-1 inhibitory activity of the previously reported 2-arylpyridothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-4-ones. All the test compounds showed highly potent pim-1 inhibition with IC50 in the range of 0.06-1.76\u2009µM. No significant difference was detected between the pim-1 inhibitory activity of the 4-pyrimidinone and the 4-imino (=NH) or the cyclised triazolopyrimidine derivatives. The most active compounds were tested for their cytotoxic activity on MCF7 and HCT116 and showed potent activity on both the cell lines."},
